<title>UK: BAe shares rise as Eurofighter worries recede.</title>
<headline>BAe shares rise as Eurofighter worries recede.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Aerospace rose 25 pence to 1232-1/2 as worries over the success of the Eurofighter project receded, dealers said.</p>
<p>BAe dropped 44 pence on Tuesday after Germany's Defence Minister Volker Ruehe declined to rule out that Germany could pull out of the project.</p>
<p>Dealers said Tuesday's fall was overdone. &quot;The nerves have steadied,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>British Aerospace is one of the partners in the multinational Eurofigher project.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
